# Evidence pages

- Path: `pathways/{domain}/{disease}/{setting}/evidence.md` (e.g. `pathways/gu/prostate/mHSPC/`)
- One disease + setting per page. Use short named sections, nested bullets, and tables only for genuinely tabular comparisons; do not merge a disease's settings into a long page.
- Purpose: scannable decision support, not a guideline dump.
- Required sections: Guidelines, Who this applies to, Standard options, Key trials / Landmark evidence, Biomarkers, Toxicity anchors, Watch list, Sources to re-check, Changelog.
- Guidelines: summarize the current NCCN, EAU, ESMO, and AUA/ASCO/SUO guidance as applicable to that disease + setting; include a published category/strength only when verified and never paste copyrighted guideline text.
- Standard options: use a risk group × option table with key inclusion and typical duration when relevant.
- Key trials / Landmark evidence: use a trial table with N, population, randomization, primary endpoint, DFS/RFS/OS HRs, and published landmark rates with years. Add a source-recreated KM-style or forest-style figure when a survival result changes practice; never reuse journal artwork or invent/digitize unreported values.
- Do not use a `Bottom line` section.
- Header fields: Last reviewed, Next review (~90 days), Owner, Purpose, Status
- Never invent trial statistics; verify or leave qualitative
- On every edit: set Last reviewed and Next review (YYYY-MM-DD) and append Changelog
- After evidence edits: `python3 scripts/build_wiki.py` so `site/` stays in sync
- Sister EpiAI project stays at `/Users/Alex/Documents/EpiAI`
